  "id": "Hackney-2026_0421",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Lower existing basement floor and create front lightwell with glass walk on roof light",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed basement extension and front lightwell/rooflight, by reason of their size, depth and detailed design, results in a disproportionate development that involves the loss of over 50% of the front garden. This fails to be subordinate to the main dwelling and would result in a disproportionate extension to the existing building.&nbsp; As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) and D4 (Delivering good design) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1 (Design Quality of Local Character) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the guidance contained within Hackney Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).",
    "The proposed basement extension, by reason of its size, detailed design, and level of excavation, results in the loss of vegetation at the site and fails to provide a areas for runoff for effective ground infiltration, facilitate planting, and support local biodiversity by way of replacement. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies G1 (Green infrastructure) and G6 (Biodiversity and access to nature) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP46 (Protection and Enhancement of Green Infrastructure) and LP47 (Biodiversity and Sites of Importance of Nature Conservation)&nbsp;of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the guidance contained within Hackney Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025).&nbsp;"
  ],
